  "guideTitle": "How SpotLink works",
  "guideSection1Title": "No internet needed",
  "guideSection1Body": "SpotLink connects directly to nearby devices over Bluetooth. Chat with friends close by even where networks are down, abroad, or in a disaster.",
  "guideSection2Title": "Friends, safely via QR",
  "guideSection2Body": "Scan a friend's code with the QR button on the Nearby tab to exchange encryption keys and become verified friends. People discovered nearby also appear automatically.",
  "guideSection3Title": "Reach farther through friends",
  "guideSection3Body": "Even beyond direct range, messages relay through other SpotLink devices in between. The radar on the Nearby tab shows who is how many hops away.",
  "guideSection4Title": "If not now, then when you meet",
  "guideSection4Body": "If someone is out of range, messages are held and delivered automatically the moment you meet again. Late arrivals show both the sent and arrival times.",
  "guideSection5Title": "Only the two of you can read it",
  "guideSection5Body": "Every message is end-to-end encrypted. Even relaying devices in the middle can't read the contents.",
  "guideSection6Title": "Battery is managed for you",
  "guideSection6Body": "When connections are stable it drops into power saving automatically, and speeds up while charging or looking for new friends. Even if the app closes, a nearby friend can wake it again.",
  "guideDontShowAgain": "Don't show again",
  "guideStart": "Get started",

